    "question": {
      ":question/id": "e23c2310-ee09-516c-87ca-27d5c2e0891d",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Without using a calculator, find the **exact** value.\n\n$$\n\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{8}\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{8}\\right)=\n$$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the cosine double-angle identity:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2\\left(x\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(x\\right)=\\cos(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstitute the angle and evaluate the standard-angle cosine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{8}\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{8}\\right) \\\\\n&= \\cos\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{7\\pi}{8}\\right) \\\\\n&= \\cos\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{4}\\right) \\\\\n&= \\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
